  "ECO372H5": "This course focuses on empirical methods used in economics to identify causal relationships. Students will learn how to interpret different model specifications, explore various identification strategies, and understand their implications for causal inference.",
  "ECO375H5": "This course is an introduction to econometrics. Statistical foundations and the interpretation of multiple regression models, with an emphasis on cross-sectional data.",
