  "MGM360H5": "This course explores the theory and process of developing compensation systems as part of an organization’s larger system for managing human potential.",
  "MGM364H5": "The role, structure, and performance of industrial relations within the framework of Canada's socio-economic-political system. Growth and history of the Canadian Labour movement: its philosophy and structure.",
  "MGM365H5": "During Human Resource Planning, organizations identify changes in human resources required to meet their future goals. In this course, students will learn about the steps involved in HR Planning including labour market forecasting, goal setting and strategic planning, and program…",
