  "PHL376H5": "Metaethics concerns the place of values in the world, and the status of ethics as a field of inquiry. Topics may include: the objectivity of morality; moral psychology; the possibility of ethical knowledge; and meanings of ethical concepts.",
  "PHL388H5": "This course explores the relationship between literature and philosophy. In addition to examining the historical tension between poets and philosophers, students will study how selected literary works, classic and contemporary, and from Western and non-Western traditions, engage…",
