  "VCC309H5": "Spectacles have been vehicles of social and political power at varying historical moments and locations. Since Guy Debord's Society of the Spectacle was published in 1967 the term has been deployed as a critical concept for thinking about visual culture.",
  "VCC334H5": "This course examines the relationship between mass media technologies and the idea of \"reality\" with an emphasis on the electronic and digital forms that dominate the discourse of \"reality\" in contemporary media culture, television, and the Internet.",
