  "WGS200H5": "This course provides an opportunity to engage in an in-depth examination of specialized and scholarly work within women and gender studies with a focus on the diverse and multidisciplinary expressions of feminist thought from the perspective of postcolonial, transnational, inters…",
  "WGS201H5": "This course provides an in-depth introduction to the interdisciplinary field of sexuality studies. Students will focus on how sexual identities and norms are shaped by cultural, historical, and social contexts.",
  "WGS202H5": "This interdisciplinary course focuses on the visions and methods that feminist scholars use to study women's and gender issues within and across a range of traditional disciplines.",
